                                        "entry_id": "34d467c3-8818-3564-841c-6bba33ccbfdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The flight of Muhammad and his followers from Mecca to Yathrib (later Medina) in 622 ce, which forms the first year of the Islamic era (ah 1)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "707cc1cd-1c98-3dca-abbe-73139584c24e",
                                        "entry_id": "34d467c3-8818-3564-841c-6bba33ccbfdb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "AH: the Islamic era, dated from the Hijra."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a92fdcab-91b3-413d-9ac8-081c4ca3e112",
                                                "sense_id": "707cc1cd-1c98-3dca-abbe-73139584c24e",
                                                "text": "Since the Muslim lunar year contains only 354 days, the year 2005 is approximately equivalent to Hijra 1426."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7e03201e-c05a-3065-90b9-84d8583f21bf",
