            {
                "entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                "word": "hégire",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "2de4f4f5-884c-41f0-aa0e-f75d3e82495c",
                        "entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "hégires"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e1f35c09-53e7-363c-b673-4583efd4754f",
                        "entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fuite de Mahomet, le prophète de l'islam, de La Mecque pour Médine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "921a0f88-b9e1-3f8a-9790-335e5f1619e4",
                        "entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Début du calendrier musulman, basé sur cet évènement."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07591ffe-08be-41ef-86cd-d43f39bdbf7c",
                                "sense_id": "921a0f88-b9e1-3f8a-9790-335e5f1619e4",
                                "text": "L’historien Khondemir prétend qu'Omar en dix ans de règne fit détruire plus de 40.000 temples chrétiens et fonda 1.400 mosquées. C'est lui qui donna l’hégire pour ère aux musulmans ; […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d9921b66-e0ff-3aba-a251-f860c55e8372",
                        "entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Calendrier musulman."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0a1eb751-c040-4f0f-a9fe-a2523898f7ec",
                                "sense_id": "d9921b66-e0ff-3aba-a251-f860c55e8372",
                                "text": "Fait à Constantinople, avec autorisation de S. H., l’année 1274 de l’Hégire."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3baf6291-9b91-42c8-afb9-b799217a5fd5",
                                "sense_id": "d9921b66-e0ff-3aba-a251-f860c55e8372",
                                "text": "La première année de l’hégire répond à l’année 622 de Jésus-Christ."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3cdfcb11-bb0f-383b-b372-50b26f4d9e10",
                        "entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Fuite, exil, en matière de religion ; début d’une nouvelle ère."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "analogy"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "83cfc4ca-6d29-452e-a854-407c6867ba52",
                                "sense_id": "3cdfcb11-bb0f-383b-b372-50b26f4d9e10",
                                "text": "Cet événement (…) fera non-seulement une époque, mais, selon bien des gens, une vraie ère chronologique dans l’histoire de la religion ; on datera désormais dans cette histoire de l’hégire jésuitique, au moins en Portugal et en France, et les jansénistes espèrent que ce nouveau comput ecclésiastique ne tardera pas à être admis dans les autres pays catholiques."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ab0c0d90-9a3b-4365-89c5-a9d2fb3fa121",
                                "sense_id": "3cdfcb11-bb0f-383b-b372-50b26f4d9e10",
                                "text": "(…) en septembre 1664 un édit avait révoqué toutes les lettres de noblesse accordées depuis 1634. Les lettres de noblesse de la famille Corneille dataient de 1637, qui est seulement l’année du Cid, hégire inconnue de l’administration."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3b00e70b-968f-4124-971c-70cc9e117eb6",
                        "source_entry_id": "2b4ab147-10e5-3f24-9e18-439da5a918aa",
                        "target_lang_word": "hijra",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hijra",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2de0ca03-f6aa-30f4-805c-b57a202c3179",
                                        "entry_id": "2850e07e-48ea-304b-a175-e4d1571240ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A eunuch in South Asia, especially one who dresses as a woman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3993d846-7d84-4581-812f-2f29c8647bc2",
                                                "sense_id": "2de0ca03-f6aa-30f4-805c-b57a202c3179",
                                                "text": "When the Mughal court was disbanded, Muslim hijras were exposed for the first time to the other, Hindu, tradition of eunuchry."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5a068a1f-1753-3e57-93fc-1bcc1c8e11e3",
                                        "entry_id": "2850e07e-48ea-304b-a175-e4d1571240ca",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A (typically biologically male or intersex, but sometimes biologically female) member of a somewhat feminine third gender found in India and Pakistan."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a696231-a695-4fa7-934e-45389c5f4b8e",
                                                "sense_id": "5a068a1f-1753-3e57-93fc-1bcc1c8e11e3",
                                                "text": "The subjects of this study are hijras or the \"third sex\" of India, individuals who occupy a unique, liminal space between male and female, sacred and profane."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2985f20-eba3-4c2b-ab25-5a079db51c62",
                                                "sense_id": "5a068a1f-1753-3e57-93fc-1bcc1c8e11e3",
                                                "text": "Even more surprisingly, there are female hijras, women who were born women, who are drawn into the gharanas by the attraction and apparent safety of the hierarchies' substitute for family life."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f430acbb-4296-4235-b95b-21425d19d35f",
                                                "sense_id": "5a068a1f-1753-3e57-93fc-1bcc1c8e11e3",
                                                "text": "While videographers were shooting him as he sat on the floor among a group of male and female sex workers, two transgender (male-to-female) hijras came to sit next to him, one on either side."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cf349165-d464-4d8a-8673-23054cc2e2fa",
                                                "sense_id": "5a068a1f-1753-3e57-93fc-1bcc1c8e11e3",
                                                "text": "Nanda profiles […] an uncastrated hijra who is married to a man and has an adopted son; and a hermaphrodite hijra […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hijra",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a2781429-c4c7-31b8-add9-088d334a8084",
                                        "entry_id": "1e5fbc26-5b6f-3fb3-8752-1f053ef0f255",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternative letter-case form of Hijra."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0a99c0cd-e9e6-323b-a7f1-92f7c6da1f16",
                                        "entry_id": "1e5fbc26-5b6f-3fb3-8752-1f053ef0f255",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any similar flight or emigration to a better place."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9f715d93-7254-3691-a262-50cdbd16da4d",
                                        "entry_id": "1e5fbc26-5b6f-3fb3-8752-1f053ef0f255",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Emigration from a non-Muslim country to a Muslim one."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b153670-5f8d-44df-b86a-4c547040b86f",
                                                "sense_id": "9f715d93-7254-3691-a262-50cdbd16da4d",
                                                "text": "Hijrah means Moving from a land of Shirk to a land of Islaam."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
